From: agent-go-trusted-platform <agent-go-trusted-platform@example.internal>
Subject: [PATCH] lib/mbedtls: return errno, not mbedTLS codes, from the parsers

pkcs7_parse_message() and x509_cert_parse() hand ERR_PTR() the raw
mbedTLS return value (for example -0x5366, MBEDTLS_ERR_PKCS7_INVALID_FORMAT
+ MBEDTLS_ERR_ASN1_LENGTH_MISMATCH). Those are below -MAX_ERRNO, so
IS_ERR() does not recognise the result and efi_image_authenticate()
dereferences it: an EFI image whose signature mbedTLS rejects takes the
firmware down with a synchronous abort instead of failing verification.

Map every mbedTLS failure to -EBADMSG before it becomes an error pointer.
Callers only test IS_ERR(); none of them distinguish the cause.

Measured on qemu_arm64 with an Authenticode signature whose
WIN_CERTIFICATE.dwLength covered two bytes of alignment padding:
"Synchronous Abort" in efi_signature_check_signers+0x28, x0 =
0xffffffffffffac9a.

--- a/lib/mbedtls/pkcs7_parser.c
+++ b/lib/mbedtls/pkcs7_parser.c
@@ -496,6 +496,13 @@ parse_fail:
 	mbedtls_pkcs7_free(&pkcs7_ctx);
 	pkcs7_free_message(msg);
 out_no_msg:
+	/*
+	 * mbedTLS codes are not errnos; below -MAX_ERRNO they pass IS_ERR()
+	 * as valid pointers and the caller dereferences them. Report every
+	 * parse failure the way the ASN.1 parser did.
+	 */
+	if (ret != -ENOMEM)
+		ret = -EBADMSG;
 	msg = ERR_PTR(ret);
 	return msg;
 }
--- a/lib/mbedtls/x509_cert_parser.c
+++ b/lib/mbedtls/x509_cert_parser.c
@@ -443,5 +443,11 @@ clean_up_ctx:
 	if (!ret)
 		return cert;
 
+	/*
+	 * See pkcs7_parse_message(): an mbedTLS code is not an errno and
+	 * would not be recognised by IS_ERR().
+	 */
+	if (ret != -ENOMEM)
+		ret = -EBADMSG;
 	return ERR_PTR(ret);
 }
